1
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:09,310
A cricket coach must pick one bowler.

2
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:14,440
These are the runs each bowler gave away per over in recent games.

3
00:00:14,490 --> 00:00:15,990
Asha: 4, 5, 4, 6, 5.

4
00:00:16,040 --> 00:00:18,020
Ben: 1, 9, 2, 8, 5.

5
00:00:18,070 --> 00:00:20,820
Which bowler is the more reliable choice?

6
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:24,060
Pause the video and choose.

7
00:00:24,110 --> 00:00:26,550
Their averages are almost the same.

8
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:31,610
But Asha's runs are always between 4 and 6, while Ben's go from 1 to 9.

9
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:36,430
Asha is more consistent, so she is the more reliable choice.

10
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:39,900
Remember: the mean is the sum divided by the count.

11
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:42,000
The median is the middle value.

12
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:43,910
The mode is the most common.

13
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:47,450
The range is the largest minus the smallest.

14
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:48,130
Your turn.

15
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:50,380
What is the range of Asha's runs?

16
00:00:50,430 --> 00:00:53,610
Pause the video and try it.

17
00:00:53,660 --> 00:00:54,680
6 minus 4 is 2.

18
00:00:54,730 --> 00:01:00,650
To compare two sets of data, compare an average, which shows how big the values are.

19
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:05,380
And compare the range, which shows how spread out they are.

20
00:01:05,430 --> 00:01:08,650
A smaller range means more consistent.

21
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:14,010
The mean uses every value, but it is pulled by extreme values, called outliers.

22
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:16,650
The median is not affected by extremes.

23
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:20,730
The mode suits categories, or the most popular size.

24
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:21,430
Your turn.

25
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:24,660
With an outlier, which average should you use?

26
00:01:24,710 --> 00:01:27,960
Pause the video and choose.

27
00:01:28,010 --> 00:01:28,720
The median.

28
00:01:28,770 --> 00:01:30,030
Here is the method.

29
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:33,970
Step 1: work out a suitable average for each set.

30
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:37,400
Step 2: work out the range for each set.

31
00:01:37,450 --> 00:01:38,590
Step 3: compare.

32
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,370
Which average is higher?

33
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:43,070
Which set is more consistent?

34
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:47,750
Step 4: write a conclusion in context, using the numbers.

35
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:53,740
Five salaries, in thousands of dollars, are 28, 30, 31, 33 and 150.

36
00:01:53,790 --> 00:01:57,220
The mean is 54.4, pulled up by the 150.

37
00:01:57,270 --> 00:02:00,790
The median is 31, which is more typical.

38
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:02,690
Use the median.

39
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:05,960
Class X has a mean of 62 and a range of 30.

40
00:02:06,010 --> 00:02:09,230
Class Y has a mean of 58 and a range of 12.

41
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:11,510
Class X did better on average.

42
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:14,880
Class Y's marks were more consistent.

43
00:02:14,930 --> 00:02:18,730
A shop sells shoes in sizes 5, 6, 6, 7, 6, 8 and 9.

44
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:21,830
Which average helps the shop order stock?

45
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:26,080
The mode, 6, because it is the most popular size.

46
00:02:26,130 --> 00:02:27,870
Team A has a range of 3.

47
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:29,750
Team B has a range of 10.

48
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:31,790
Which line is wrong?

49
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:32,910
Line 1 is wrong.

50
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:35,420
The range measures spread, not size.

51
00:02:35,470 --> 00:02:37,230
Team B is less consistent.

52
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:40,430
Use an average to say who scores more.

53
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:43,340
Team B's scores are more spread out.

54
00:02:43,390 --> 00:02:47,610
News reports usually give the median house price, not the mean.

55
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:54,990
A few very expensive houses would pull the mean up, and make prices look higher than most people pay.

56
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:56,100
One last question.

57
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:58,240
What does the range tell you about?

58
00:02:58,290 --> 00:03:01,290
Pause the video and choose.

59
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:05,090
The range tells you about the spread of the data.

60
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:08,840
To remember: compare an average, and the range.

61
00:03:08,890 --> 00:03:12,040
A smaller range means more consistent.

62
00:03:12,090 --> 00:03:14,060
The median resists outliers.

63
00:03:14,110 --> 00:03:16,480
The mode suits categories.

64
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:20,290
Write your conclusion in context, with numbers.

65
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:25,710
Great work! Now practise lesson 16.6 on Camday.
